t=t[:start]+'''IoErrorKind is exactly `permission-denied`, `no-space`, `io-error`, `other`. For an actual returned io::Error, map ErrorKind::PermissionDenied first, StorageFull second; then any remaining error with an actual raw_os_error to io-error; every remaining actual error maps other. This complete stable mapping does not name Rust's unstable Uncategorized variant or hardcode cross-platform EIO values. Darwin EACCES/ENOSPC/EIO observations are evidence for this host only; Linux controls remain owed. Errno is independently K2-admitted only from the SAME actual returned native error and omitted when absent. Never format Error/Display/message or accept a worker/caller label.

A successful returned count smaller than the requested syscall unit is a short write, not an io::Error, and contributes no fabricated sink_error or errno. Its continuation still needs its own successful gate admission. Delivered complete records stay written; a remainder denied continuation is sink-stopped; a later actual I/O error has its own existing sink-failed outcome. An actual WriteZero io::Error without a native code maps other. Returned counts outside 0..requested are an actual host invariant, not other. If no actual I/O error occurs, both optional sink_error and errno are omitted, even if a short write recovered or a gate closed. The first ACTUAL I/O error and same error's admitted errno are carried in that writer's immutable cumulative snapshot at its owning exchange and frozen from that cell, never a separate late gauge or pair fabricated from two observations. This preserves the existing first-I/O-error meaning; the short-write controls test the distinct continuation law and require no new error-table member.
''' +t[end:];(D/'CONTRACT.md').write_text(t)
r=(D/'RECOMMENDATION.md').read_text();start=r.index('IoErrorKind ');end=r.index('\n\nThese mappings',start);r=r[:start]+'''IoErrorKind now proposes four closed members: permission-denied (PermissionDenied), no-space (StorageFull), io-error (every other actual returned error with raw_os_error present), and other (remaining actual returned errors). The Darwin probe shows EIO is Uncategorized, so neither unstable variant matching nor Other alone gives a complete portable mapping. A successful short-write count is not an I/O error; it remains in the existing continuation/gate accounting with no fabricated sink_error or errno. The first actual error/errno pair stays in the same immutable writer snapshot. Exact field spellings are sink_error and errno, not guessed aliases.''' +r[end:];(D/'RECOMMENDATION.md').write_text(r)
